A||||7||JAMIE||centre caps on 88GT wheels||||1||
Z||000000||JAMIE||01-17-2001||11:13 AM||||Anyone know if the centre caps with the Fiero logo were offered on the 1988GT's , or, were only the plain centres offered.Both my 88GT's have plain centres.Anyone with an 88GT out there that has logo centre caps?<P>Thanks<P>Jamie||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||01-17-2001||12:03 PM||||88 GT's had plain center caps.  The 86 & 87 GT had a Fiero pegesas within the shield emblem on the center cap, like the nose badge.  NOS caps with emblems are rather pricy.  Rodney Dickman sells an applique of the design, which can be stuck to the plain cap.  Unless you are anal and look real close, you cannot tell the difference.  He even has one like the GT nose badge, which says Fiero GT.||||reg||3
Z||000002||JAMIE||01-17-2001||04:03 PM||||Old Lar<P>Thanks for the info.<P>Regards<P>Jamie||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fformula88||01-17-2001||07:24 PM||||I picked up a set of new ones from the Fiero Store (Genuine GM parts too!).  I think I paid about $20 a piece for them, but am very pleased.  My old ones had totally corroded over and totally useless.  I have also seen Rodney's stickers on Fiero caps and they look good too.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Black88GT||01-18-2001||12:10 PM||||My '88 GT has gold wheels, and the center cap is black with a gold Fiero GT logo on it.  At a recent MAFOA meeting, 2 guys there had gold wheels but with silver centers.  I always wondered if mine were stock or they just lost there's or something...<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000005||My7Fieros||01-18-2001||12:23 PM||||I used Rodney Dickmans center cap stickers...they look GREAT! Thumbs up for Rodney!||||reg||14
Z||000006||Old Lar||01-18-2001||12:36 PM||||You can get the plain center caps from GM for a lot less than $20 each, then use Rodneys stickers for the look.||||reg||3
